    "body": "@domenic Can you elaborate? How to prevent data loss via service workers + background sync, if the unloading happens immediately after a modification?\n\nIf the user decide to clear his/her storage then that is his/her decision (no difference for native apps). I'm not aware of a UA may clear IndexedDB without users' permission -- well UA may actually do that, but since the quota is fairly large, the probalility is low. Some UA also support persistant storages, though not quite standard.\n\n@igrigorik If a user close a foreground page which contains unsaved data, I think visibility change won't happen.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
