    "created_at": "2016-03-30T18:52:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-30T18:52:46Z",
    "body": "I don't think we can make any hard guarantees about \"finish\", regardless of whether you're talking about visibilitychange or beforeunload -- e.g. if you fire a bunch of sync XHRs, or spin a while loop for 10 minutes.. that's a problem, and I'd fully expect some browsers to kill or disallow such behaviors. That said, if the operations are async and finish reasonably quickly.. then, yes.\n",
